# The portable suite plus the hxcpp-only suite. Run from the repository root.
#
#   haxe test/cpp/build.hxml && ./bin_test/cpp/common/AllCommon.exe && ./bin_test/cpp/cppia/AllCpp.exe
#
# The reference target: hxcpp is what ships, and the coercion and DCE behaviour the library cares
# about is its behaviour.
-cp src
-cp test/common
-cp test/common/fixtures
-cp test/lib
# The library ships with this applied via extraParams.hxml (`-lib hxscript`). The suite uses
# `-cp src`, which does not read extraParams, so without this line the suite tests a
# configuration no consumer builds: under the default -dce std the standard-library members a
# script reaches by reflection are stripped, and EReg loses its methods.
--macro hxscript.macro.Keep.run()
# The bridged base and the kept fixtures, exactly as `test/lib/conformance.sh` sets them. Without
# them the corpus's host-property cases cannot resolve `HostBase` and report `Type not found`,
# which is a fact about this build rather than about the library. They were added to the corpus
# and not here, and nothing ran the whole matrix afterwards, so five cases sat failing.
--macro hxscript.setup.Autowire.run()
-D hxscript_bridge_types=HostBase,HostQuirk,HostShaped
-D hxscript_keep=haxe.Json,haxe.ds.Option,HostVec,HostVecImpl,HostFlag,HostDial,HostTint

-main AllCommon
-cpp bin_test/cpp/common

--next

# The cppia suite. `-D scriptable` and `-dce no` are not tuning: cppia resolves the host's classes by
# name at load time, and DCE removes whatever no compiled call site references.
-cp src
-cp test/common
-cp test/common/fixtures
-cp test/lib
-cp test/cpp
-D scriptable
-D hxscript_cppia
-dce no
--macro hxscript.macro.Keep.run()
# The bridged base and the kept fixtures, exactly as `test/lib/conformance.sh` sets them. Without
# them the corpus's host-property cases cannot resolve `HostBase` and report `Type not found`,
# which is a fact about this build rather than about the library. They were added to the corpus
# and not here, and nothing ran the whole matrix afterwards, so five cases sat failing.
--macro hxscript.setup.Autowire.run()
-D hxscript_bridge_types=HostBase,HostQuirk,HostShaped
-D hxscript_keep=haxe.Json,haxe.ds.Option,HostVec,HostVecImpl,HostFlag,HostDial,HostTint

-main AllCpp
-cpp bin_test/cpp/cppia

--next

# The frontier instrument, its own program because it is not a gate: see test/lib/Frontier.hx.
-cp src
-cp test/common
-cp test/common/fixtures
-cp test/lib
-cp test/cpp
-D scriptable
-D hxscript_cppia
-dce no
--macro hxscript.macro.Keep.run()
# The bridged base and the kept fixtures, exactly as `test/lib/conformance.sh` sets them. Without
# them the corpus's host-property cases cannot resolve `HostBase` and report `Type not found`,
# which is a fact about this build rather than about the library. They were added to the corpus
# and not here, and nothing ran the whole matrix afterwards, so five cases sat failing.
--macro hxscript.setup.Autowire.run()
-D hxscript_bridge_types=HostBase,HostQuirk,HostShaped
-D hxscript_keep=haxe.Json,haxe.ds.Option,HostVec,HostVecImpl,HostFlag,HostDial,HostTint

-main FrontierTest
-cpp bin_test/cppia
